.TH PSDotVM 3 2023-12-09 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSDotVM\fR \- vector\-matrix multiplication

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
int  
.br
\fBPSDotVM\fR(\fIPSFloat *a\fR, \fIPSMatrix b\fR, \fIPSMatrix dest\fR, \fIPSMathOpts *opts\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Perform vector-matrix multiplication by calling \fIPSDot\fR and setting \fIargtype\fR member of \fIopts\fR to `argtype[0] = 'V', argtype[1] = 'M'`.
.br
See \fIPSDot\fR for a more detailed description.
.br

.br
\fBNOTE\fR:  \fIopts\fR argument is optional, and if given, it's never overwritten by the function since its values are copied to a local structure.
.br

.SH RETURN VALUES
See \fIPSDot\fR.

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1), PSDot(3)
